# Macros named *_MAX_* or *_LIMIT* that are not limits a user can reach, so they have no row in SIFT_LIMITS (src/core/limits.h).
# NAME, a tab, the reason. scripts/gen-limits.sh --check fails for a macro that is neither here nor a row, and for a line whose macro is gone.
# A bound that a user can reach gets a row, not a line here.
DENSE_MAX_CLASSES	the tuples of column values a dense lookup table tells apart (agg/lookcol.c): past it the table is hashed row by row and the rows are the same
ARR_MAX_CANDS	array columns whose elements the default of paths samples: a memory bound of the sample (128 MB of sets), the others keep their image
CHUNK_MAX_N	sanity bound on the row count a decoder reads from a chunk: a corruption check
COL_MAX_WIDE	array size that mirrors wide_conjuncts (SIFT_AGG_MAX_WIDE)
ESTIMATE_MEMO_MAX_KEY	size of the key of a planner memo: an internal cache bound with no visible effect
INLINE_JOIN_LIMIT	width of the join-order search of the inline plan of a shared CTE: a planning-cost choice with no visible limit (the plan differs, the rows do not)
MERGE_MAX_BYTES	no caller left: delete it in a cleanup
ORDER_MAX_ROWS	the most rows of a key-cut unit, the maximum of sift.col_unit_rows (the directory of a unit is read with the head of its record)
PAGG_MAX_TUPLES	decoder bound for a rollup blob (a corruption check), derived from rollup_tuples
POOL_MAX_BLOCKS	size of the CREATE INDEX buffer pool, kept so that addresses stay below 2^32 (sift.test_pool_blocks lowers it)
PROBE_MAX_ENTRIES	size of the table of one planner probe: an internal bound with no visible effect
RANK_MAX_ROWS	most rows the SiftSort node ranks in memory: more go to the tuplesort, as a Sort sorts them (the rows are the same, the packed rank keys of 40 million rows are 320 MB)
SIFT_AGG_MAX_PARAMS	derived array size of the executor parameters
SIFT_ALLOC_MAX_LOCKED	invariant of the block allocator, not reachable by valid input
SIFT_COLSTUB_MAX_STR	test-only stub source (SIFT_TESTING)
SIFT_COL_FORMAT_MAX_READ	the newest column format minor this build reads: a version, not a size
SIFT_COL_MAX_LANES	array size of the lanes of one numeric leaf
SIFT_CORDER_MAX_KEYS	an IN list of more keys than this is read from the units: each key seeks a chunk of the sorted keys of its own
SIFT_CORDER_MAX_ROWS	a range of more rows than this is read from the units: the addresses of a range are sorted by position before the heap is read
SIFT_CPOINT_MAX_KEYS	keys of one lookup that the point directory answers: a speed threshold, the answer is the same either way
SIFT_CPOINT_MAX_RANGE	keys of one range that the point directory enumerates: a speed threshold, the zones answer a longer range the same way
SIFT_CPOINT_MAX_ROWS	rows of one lookup that the point directory answers: a speed threshold, the answer is the same either way
SIFT_FOLD_MAX_EXPAND	characters one character expands to in case folding: a property of the Unicode tables
SIFT_MAX_EXTENTS	derived from the page layout (extents of a segment header)
SIFT_MAX_OFF	width of a page bitmap: the layout of the postings
SIFT_MAX_OFFSET	MaxHeapTuplesPerPage, a PostgreSQL bound
SIFT_MAX_REBINDS	size of the table of kernel rebind callbacks
SIFT_MAX_W	words of a page bitmap: the layout of the postings
SIFT_MERGE_MAX_FANIN	merge policy: segments one merge reads at a time
SIFT_MERGE_MAX_SEGMENTS	merge policy: more directory entries than this start a merge
SIFT_NUM_MAX_DIGITS	the same limit as wide_digits, counted by the planner
SIFT_RADIX_MAX_DIGIT	bits of the widest digit of the radix sort of core/cmp.h: the counters of a digit (4 KB) and the cache lines its pass writes to; the order of the result does not depend on it
SIFT_SRC_MAX_DIMS	planner-side array size of the dimensions of a source, above cube_dims
SIFT_SRC_MAX_MEAS	planner-side array size that mirrors cube_measures
SIFT_SRC_MAX_RDIMS	planner-side array size that mirrors rollup_dims
SIFT_SRC_MAX_ROLLUPS	planner-side array size that mirrors rollups
SIFT_TBL_MAX_OFF	MaxHeapTuplesPerPage, a PostgreSQL bound
SIFT_TBL_MAX_WBUF_PAGES	array size of the page list of one write buffer: see write_buffer_kb and tx_write_buffers
SIFT_TBL_ROW_MAX_INLINE	a sift_table row above half a page goes to overflow pages: a layout threshold, not a limit
SIFT_KTAB_MAX_GROUPS	the keys of a leaf in a segment beyond which the accumulator of its key table stops: a memory bound, a table that large takes more than 3% of any segment
SIFT_VK_MAX_GROUPS	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
SIFT_VK_MAX_PRED	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
SIFT_VK_MAX_RS	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
SIFT_VK_MAX_SLOTS	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
SIFT_VK_MAX_SUM	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
SIFT_VK_MAX_UNITS	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
VK_MAX_MEMORY_HEAPS	constant of the Vulkan API
VK_MAX_MEMORY_TYPES	constant of the Vulkan API
VK_MAX_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_NAME_SIZE	constant of the Vulkan API
VSHM_MAX_SETS	the array of the shared verdict table, which sift.verdict_cache_kb (up to 1 MB) fills in part
CAL_MAX_CUTS	the most clock changes of the session zone the prefilter of a periodic calendar step splits its windows at (a span of several centuries); more and the step is tested by the expression, no result changes
LOAD_MAX_GROUPS	groups a bulk load writes at once: the backend and three workers, bounded by max_parallel_maintenance_workers and maintenance_work_mem
LOAD_MAX_UNITS	array size of the units of a run: LOAD_SBS for each of LOAD_MAX_GROUPS
DP_MAX_LEVELS	size of the array of the pages of one descent: a btree is never as deep, the probe falls back to the index scan when it is
DP_MAX_PEND	keys of a chunk the direct probe holds before it flushes them: a memory bound of the batch with no visible effect
JSTR_MAX_KEYS	a text join key list longer than this, or than a sixteenth of the table's rows, is left to the join: a speed threshold, the rows are the same either way
SIFT_CONN_MAX_CONNECTIONS	connections one connect option names: a syntax bound of the option text, rejected with an error
FOUND_MAX_KEYS	keys the journal of a parent may name for a join answered from the found flag (agg/found.c): past it the join loads the parent, the rows are the same
FOUND_MAX_PROBES	keys deleted or changed in a parent that a join answered from the found flag probes in its btree (agg/found.c): past it the join loads the parent, the rows are the same
CONN_TAGS_MAX_KEYS	the keys of a read past which its journal records are not filtered by their key tag (the tags of that many keys leave few records out): a cost bound, the rows are the same
BLK_SLOTS	layout: the offsets of one scoring block, SIFT_BLK_PAGES pages of SIFT_KERN_SLOTS
SIFT_KERN_SLOTS	layout: the offsets of one heap page in the offset mask (SIFT_OFFMASK_WORDS words of 64 bits)
CUBE_SET_SLOTS	size of the probe table of one histogram dimension, a power of two over twice its groups (col/keycols/cube.c); the table is local to the call
ROWS_SLOTS	size of the probe table that counts the distinct pairs of a stretch, a power of two over the cells a unit may keep; it stops counting at its limit
PAGG_SLOTS	size of the probe table of the histogram sizing of the autocut (col/autocut/size.c); the table is local to the call
DENSE_SLOTS	size of the hash over the classes of a dense lookup table, four times DENSE_MAX_CLASSES; past DENSE_MAX_CLASSES the table is hashed row by row
F_SLOTS	a flag bit of a shared dictionary (the slots form), not a size
KEYS_DENSE_SLOTS	slots a key needs in a bitmap before a sorted array is used instead: a speed threshold, the keys are the same
MEMO_SLOTS	slots of the memo of the rows of a child scan that a query shares between its workers (agg/memo.c): an entry is stored only while the table is half full and the 32 MB arena has room, the others are computed again
NDICT_SLOTS	dictionaries an aggregate scan keeps open at one time (agg/leaf.c): the least recently used one is replaced
PEND_SLOTS	indexes whose rows a backend buffers for one commit (col/wbuf/pending.c): the rows of another index are written to its lane at once
PROBE_AHEAD_SLOTS	slots above which the group probe prefetches (agg/group/gids.c): a speed threshold, the groups are the same
SET_MEMO_SLOTS	entries of the memo of the ranges of one probe, replaced in turn (col/amscan/ranges.c)
TOMB_SLOTS	indexes whose tombstones a statement holds back for the page-wise append (col/supersede.c): when none is free every held buffer goes to the log and the first is reused
SIFT_TOMB_PRESSURE_ENTRIES	the length of the tombstone log of a sift_table at which the maintenance worker is asked for: a scheduling threshold, with no effect on what a statement may do
SIFT_TOMB_SYNC_ENTRIES	the length of the tombstone log of a sift_table past which a ticking backend leaves the count of its tombstones to the worker: a scheduling threshold, with no effect on what a statement may do
SIDE_MAX_CELLS	months of one run of the scope sidecar that keep their own cube: a run of more keeps the cube of all its rows only, and the reads of it are by reference (col/seg_write/side.c); a size bound of the summary with no other effect
SIFT_COL_BTREE_WORKERS	participants of a build through a btree on the key at most (the directory holds the segments of each): a share of the directory, not a size a table may reach (col/build/btree_par.c)
SIM_MAX_BLOCKS	blocks the cache of the choice between the btree and the key ranges simulates at most (the cache is scaled down by a power of two to it): bounds the memory of the walk, not what a table may hold (col/build/btree_pick.c)
COST_MIN_US	the range (microseconds) a measured cost of a read of the heap is held to by the choice between a btree on the key and the key ranges (col/build/btree_probe.c): a read of a page in the memory of the system and a seek of a disk that spins; a noise bound of the measurement, not a size a table may reach
COST_MAX_US	the upper end of that range
PRICE_BYTES	bytes of rows the pricing of the key ranges' files may take (col/build/spill.c): bounds the memory of the pricing, not what a table may reach
